From 0b3b152beb2aa13842f8c2841ce4bb3ca418d1d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Belkin <anton.belkin@icloud.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:27:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] mac: log the time from input to the screen with
 --macos-latency-log

For each frame shown through the swapchain, a line in the latency
module with the time of the input it shows (afp_input_time, which the
script that turns gestures into shader parameters puts in
--glsl-shader-opts), the newest input when the VO began drawing it,
when it began, got its drawable, went to the swapchain and was shown
(the drawable's presentedTime), all on the host clock. The trackpad's
gesture messages carry their event's time last, so a script can pass
it on. --macos-latency-test makes up a two-finger scroll at a given
rate, for measuring without a trackpad.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
