-    only while it needs them.
+    only while it needs them. Each message ends with its event's time, in seconds of the host
+    clock (as ``NSEvent.timestamp``), after the phase.
+
+``--macos-latency-log=<yes|no>``
+    Logs, for each frame shown through the swapchain, how long ago the input it shows came in
+    (default: no): a line ``frame=<n> applied=<t> newest=<t> begin=<t> drawable=<t> submit=<t>
+    shown=<t>`` in the ``latency`` module, at info level, the times in seconds of the host clock
+    (as ``NSEvent.timestamp`` and a drawable's ``presentedTime``). ``applied`` is the time of the
+    input the frame shows, as a script turning gestures into shader parameters gives it in
+    ``--glsl-shader-opts`` as ``afp_input_time`` (the gestures' script messages carry their event's
+    time last); ``newest`` the newest input event when the VO began drawing it, ``begin`` then,
+    ``drawable`` when the frame got the Metal layer's drawable, ``submit`` when it went to the
+    swapchain and ``shown`` when it was on screen (0: never).
+
+``--macos-latency-test=<0-1000>``
+    Makes up a two-finger scroll of 4 points this many times a second, a second to the right and a
+    second to the left, while ``--macos-gesture-messages`` is on, each timed as it's sent (default:
+    0, none). For measuring with ``--macos-latency-log`` without a trackpad.
 
